 "dur": 45.0,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Henrik built his roof so steep, his goat slid off it twice.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.184
  },
  {
   "text": "You see, in Frostdal, three meters of snow fall every winter.",
   "s": 3.384,
   "e": 6.524
  },
  {
   "text": "His neighbor Sven laughed: \"Is that a house, or a party hat?\"",
   "s": 6.724,
   "e": 9.576
  },
  {
   "text": "Sven's roof was flat, with a hot tub on top. All autumn, he soaked.",
   "s": 9.696,
   "e": 13.161
  },
  {
   "text": "Then came three storms. Storm one: half a meter. Sven waved.",
   "s": 13.361,
   "e": 16.591
  },
  {
   "text": "Storm two: two meters. His beams creaked, but Sven grinned: \"Strong roof!\"",
   "s": 16.791,
   "e": 20.471
  },
  {
   "text": "Storm three: wet snow, each square meter as heavy as four men.",
   "s": 20.591,
   "e": 23.58
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the roof sagged, and Sven's door jammed shut.",
   "s": 23.98,
   "e": 26.125
  },
  {
   "text": "Ever sat at the top of a steep slide? You can't stay up there.",
   "s": 26.325,
   "e": 29.296
  },
  {
   "text": "Neither can snow. So on a steep roof, it slides off before it gets heavy.",
   "s": 29.495,
   "e": 33.112
  },
  {
   "text": "Whump! Henrik's roof shrugged off its snow and stood dry.",
   "s": 33.312,
   "e": 35.76
  },
  {
   "text": "Sven climbed out his window and begged: \"Can I sleep at yours?\"",
   "s": 35.96,
   "e": 38.975
  },
  {
   "text": "Henrik handed him a tiny party hat. The goat already had one.",
   "s": 39.095,
   "e": 42.601
  }
 ],
